At Tue, 5 Aug 2003 16:08:27 +0200,
juan wrote:
> 
> On Tuesday 05 August, 2003 ? 03:58:34PM +0200, Takashi Iwai wrote:
> > At Sun, 3 Aug 2003 23:02:37 +0200,
> > juan loco wrote:
> > > 
> > > i have a dell c600 laptop running kernel 2.4.21
> > > 
> > > when i load the maestro driver , my system hangs 2 seconds later.
> > > 
> > > i tried 2.4.20 / 2.6.0-test , same problem
> > 
> > is ACPI enabled?
> > 
> i tried with/without preempt and acpi , same hardware freeze
> how can i trace the problem ? it's hard since the machines dies :(

do you see the LED blinking?
if yes, you could see a last kernel dieing message in the log terminal
(often alt+F10 in linux console).  try to switch to that one quickly
after loading the module, and wait for the death.  if sysrq is enabled
in the kernel, you can see even the backtrace via alt+sysrq+P.


Takashi


